// A local's C type must not outlive its function body.
//
// `_localCTypes` (local/param -> full C type) was cleared in exactly ONE place — the `parallel_for`
// worker synthesis — while the four per-body resets cleared its siblings (`_localTypes`,
// `_localTypeNodes`, `_constLocals`, `_constLocalVals`) and skipped it. So a local's C type leaked
// from one body into the next, and `lvalueCType` consults that map BEFORE the field lookup: a stale
// entry shadows a same-named field of a different type in a later body.
//
// Here `A.seed` leaves a `string v`; `B.set` then assigns to B's OWN field `v`, an `int32`. The
// assignment handler read the stale `kama_string` and rejected this program with
// "a collection/`string` hand-off must say `give` (move) or `copy` (deep)" — an ownership diagnostic
// on an `int32 = int32` assignment, pointing at code that is correct. Valid code, refused.
type value A {
    int32 pad;
    public ctor make() { this.pad = 0; }
    public fn void seed() { string v = "hello"; }
}

type value B {
    int32 v;
    public ctor make() { this.v = 0; }
    public fn void set(int32 n) { v = n; }
    public fn int32 get() { return this.v; }
}

fn int32 main() {
    A a = A.make();
    a.seed();
    B b = B.make();
    b.set(n: 42);
    return b.get();
}
